Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:07.50,Accent,,0,0,0,,{\b1}CIPHER LENS{\b0}  |  AI Agent for Automated Penetration Testing
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.50,0:00:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 1: Authorized Scope Registration{\b0} — Targets, ports, and strict exclusions are locked down before any tool runs.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.64,0:00:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Mandatory human attestation ensures only authorized lab environments can be targeted.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.64,0:00:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Scope token {\b1}#190e6f7f{\b0} generated with SHA-256 integrity hashing to lock engagement boundaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.00,0:00:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 2: Conversational Intake{\b0} — The analyst describes the objective in plain English without command-line flags.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The dual-model AI planner (Google Gemini) evaluates registered scope and prior evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.64,0:01:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,AI proposes Nmap service discovery. Safety gate verifies port and rate limits before sandboxed execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.64,0:01:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 3: Approved Scanning{\b0} — Nmap runs in a secure sandbox; raw XML is ingested to evidence vault.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.00,0:01:17.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Port 80 confirmed open running Apache httpd. Finding recorded with raw evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.64,0:01:26.87,Accent,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 4: Adaptive Planning{\b0} — Next step adapts dynamically using newly observed Nmap evidence to target Apache.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.87,0:01:36.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Nikto web configuration scan executes against confirmed HTTP service, detecting outdated components and header flaws.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.87,0:01:42.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 5: Web Application Mapping{\b0} — OWASP ZAP spider crawls endpoints to build the target site tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.89,0:01:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Findings workbench aggregates evidence: anti-clickjacking headers, HTTP TRACE, and server version disclosures.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.92,0:02:08.00,Accent,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 6: The Human Approval Gateway{\b0} — Active & offensive actions carry real operational risk that AI must never trigger alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.00,0:02:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Autonomous AI is blocked by policy gate. Junior analyst submits an explicit approval request for ZAP active scanning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.00,0:02:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Senior analyst reviews scope and grants time-limited 15-minute token {\b1}#3d91bb7d{\b0}, recorded in audit chain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.92,0:02:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 7: Gated Active Validation{\b0} — ZAP active scan executes with verified authorization token, validating vulnerabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.92,0:02:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 8: Multi-Tool Ingestion{\b0} — External Nessus report parsed; findings jump to 26 with CVSS 10.0 and CVE enrichment.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.92,0:03:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Severe vulnerabilities surfaced: Samba command execution (CVE-2007-2447), Debian OpenSSH flaw, and backdoor shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.92,0:03:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,OpenVAS report ingested. Cross-tool correlation engine deduplicates findings and maps to MITRE ATT&CK framework.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.84,0:03:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Step 9: Integration Truth{\b0} — Honest capability matrix disclosing 3 Live, 3 Import-Only, and 1 Planned tool adapter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.84,0:03:49.34,Accent,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Final Deliverable{\b0} — Professional 11-page executive VAPT report generated with ReportLab: verified and client-ready.
